; Specification section 8.5. A string prints double-quoted, escaping exactly
; what has to be escaped for the same text to read back and nothing else. A
; letter which is not ASCII is written as itself, and because a line feed is
; escaped, canonical form never holds a raw line break inside a string.
(project
  (label "Grünstraße 12, 一メートル")
  (globalid-namespace "https://example.org/models/riverside")
  (description "A \"quoted\" phrase, a back\\slash, a\ttab and a\nline break."))
(namespace survey (description "Control \u0007 issued by Acme Surveys."))
(node site:S-101 (label "") (kind Space) (type MeetingRoom))
